# Universal Versioning

RULE: ALL repos (libraries, services, UIs) use semver. Every main merge bumps version. Version tag = Docker image tag = immutable reference.
WHY: Cloud Build fails if library version exists with different commit; prevents stale packages. Immutable tags enable safe rollbacks.
CODEX: 05-infrastructure/versioning-rollback.md, 06-coding-standards/quality-gates.md

DO:
- Bump version in pyproject.toml/package.json before changing code in unified-* libraries
- Every main merge bumps version (quality gates enforce for libraries; convention for services/UIs)
- Deploy by version tag only (never SHA or latest)
- Branch builds: tagged with branch-name-sha, not semver; auto-routed to dev project

NEVER:
- Change code then bump; reuse version with different commit
- Deploy by SHA or latest
- Bump version on branches (branch images use branch-name-sha tag)
